//- FAQ
//- ============================================================
section(class="bg-bg-subtle/40")
	.max-w-3xl.mx-auto.px-6.py-20
		.text-center.mb-10
			Badge(variant="info" class="mb-3") FAQ
			h2.text-3xl.font-bold.tracking-tight.mb-3(class="md:text-4xl") Common questions
		+snippet('faq1')
			p.text-sm(class="text-fg-muted")
				| Yes. Norns sits on top of SvelteKit — every adapter, hook, and form action keeps working.
				| You can use
				code .svelte
				| and
				code .n
				| files side-by-side in the same app.
		+snippet('faq2')
			p.text-sm(class="text-fg-muted")
				| Civet compiles to standard ESM, so Svelte 5's runes, derived state, and effects work without preprocessing tricks.
		+snippet('faq3')
			p.text-sm(class="text-fg-muted")
				| MIT. Use it commercially, fork it, vendor it — no strings attached.
		+snippet('faq4')
			p.text-sm(class="text-fg-muted")
				| You can. The
				code &lt;Btn href="/url"&gt;
				| polymorphic pattern, role-token CSS, and behaviors module are usable as plain Svelte+TS too.
		+snippet('faq5')
			p.text-sm(class="text-fg-muted")
				| Hooks are wired up but the production deploy story is still firming up. Stable 1.0 is targeted later this year.
		Accordion(items!="{faqItems(faq1, faq2, faq3, faq4, faq5)}")

